# RPi Manual Deploy Instructions (No Scripts)

Use this when laptop + Raspberry Pi are on the same Wi-Fi.

## 1) On laptop, go to project and confirm release exists

```bash
cd /Users/sozodennis/Developer/fprime-artemis-cubesat/ArtemisRpiTeensy_N2
ls -la releases/release-20260213-223835-63e1b5b-armhf
```

Expected files:
- `ArtemisRpiTeensyDeployment`
- `ArtemisRpiTeensyDeploymentTopologyDictionary.json`
- `SHA256SUMS`
- `RELEASE_INFO.txt`

## 2) Find Raspberry Pi IP on local Wi-Fi

Try mDNS first:

```bash
ping -c 1 raspberrypi.local
```

If that works, use `raspberrypi.local` as host.  
If not, scan local ARP table:

```bash
arp -a | grep -i raspberry
```

If still not found, get your subnet and probe it:

```bash
ipconfig getifaddr en0
```

If laptop IP is like `192.168.188.X`, check likely Pi hostnames:

```bash
for i in {2..254}; do ping -c 1 -W 100 192.168.188.$i >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo "up: 192.168.188.$i"; done
```

Then test SSH:

```bash
ssh pi@<PI_IP>
```

Default student account assumed: `pi` (password is whatever was set on that Pi image).

## 3) Create target folders on Pi

```bash
ssh pi@<PI_IP> "mkdir -p /home/pi/artemis/releases /home/pi/artemis/current /home/pi/artemis/logs"
```

## 4) SCP release from laptop to Pi

```bash
scp -r /Users/sozodennis/Developer/fprime-artemis-cubesat/ArtemisRpiTeensy_N2/releases/release-20260213-223835-63e1b5b-armhf pi@<PI_IP>:/home/pi/artemis/releases/
```

## 5) Activate that release on Pi

```bash
ssh pi@<PI_IP> '
set -e
BASE=/home/pi/artemis
REL=$BASE/releases/release-20260213-223835-63e1b5b-armhf
chmod +x "$REL/ArtemisRpiTeensyDeployment"
ln -sfn "$REL" "$BASE/active_release"
ln -sfn "$BASE/active_release/ArtemisRpiTeensyDeployment" "$BASE/current/ArtemisRpiTeensyDeployment"
ln -sfn "$BASE/active_release/ArtemisRpiTeensyDeploymentTopologyDictionary.json" "$BASE/current/ArtemisRpiTeensyDeploymentTopologyDictionary.json"
echo release-20260213-223835-63e1b5b-armhf > "$BASE/active_release_name.txt"
echo "Activated: $(cat "$BASE/active_release_name.txt")"
'
```

## 6) (Recommended) Verify checksums on Pi

```bash
ssh pi@<PI_IP> '
cd /home/pi/artemis/active_release
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
'
```

Expected: `OK` for each file.

## 7) Run the deployment (foreground test)

```bash
ssh pi@<PI_IP> '/home/pi/artemis/current/ArtemisRpiTeensyDeployment -d /dev/serial0'
```

Stop with `Ctrl+C`.

## 8) Run in background with log

```bash
ssh pi@<PI_IP> '
nohup /home/pi/artemis/current/ArtemisRpiTeensyDeployment -d /dev/serial0 \
  > /home/pi/artemis/logs/flight.log 2>&1 &
echo "PID: $!"
'
```

Check process/log:

```bash
ssh pi@<PI_IP> 'pgrep -af ArtemisRpiTeensyDeployment; tail -n 50 /home/pi/artemis/logs/flight.log'
```

